---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pagePath = '/image-policy/';
const description =
  'How Pick Your Row uses AI generated cabin and aircraft photographs, and where the Image policy link under those images leads.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Image policy',
  description,
  url: `https://pickyourrow.com${pagePath}`,
  dateModified: '2026-11-19',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  isPartOf: {
    '@type': 'WebSite',
    name: 'Pick Your Row',
    url: 'https://pickyourrow.com/',
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Pick Your Row',
    url: 'https://pickyourrow.com/',
  },
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Image policy"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath={pagePath}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Image policy</nav>
    <h1 class="page-title">Image policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Last updated: 19 November 2026</p>
    <p>
      This page explains how Pick Your Row uses pictures. Ownership details are on the
      <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> page. Questions about an image can be sent through the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>AI generated photographs</h2>
    <p>
      The photographs and photo style illustrations on this site are AI generated images. They are not
      photographs of a specific airline cabin, airport, or aircraft registration, and they are not pictures of
      real people as they appeared. They are decorative illustrations that sit beside seat maps and guides. A
      caption under each of these images says that it is an AI generated illustration and includes a link back to
      this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Seat map schematics</h2>
    <p>
      Seat diagrams are separate from the photographs. They are original SVG schematics drawn from publicly known
      typical configuration facts. They are labelled as illustrative and can differ by registration. Confirm the
      layout for your flight with the airline. How those drawings are made is explained on the
      <a href="/methodology/">Methodology and sources</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Concept cabin renders</h2>
    <p>
      A few guides show speculative cabin concepts. Those images are labelled as concept art or AI concept renders.
      They are design briefs, not certified products and not booking advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Credits and questions</h2>
    <p>
      If a licensed or Creative Commons photograph is added later, its caption will name the source. Until then,
      treat every photo style image on this site as an AI generated illustration and use this page as the source
      credit. If you have a question about an image, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      See also our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>, <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>,
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>, and <a href="/methodology/">Methodology and sources</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
